From b3c83a1c876f5305fe45b2d812ba330d1f1bef22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joeri Van Dooren <ure@on6ure.be>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] app: an abort while Pat waits for a clear channel ends the
 dial at once (OpenX6X00)

ARDOP's and VARA's dialers wait for a clear channel through the busy
function (onBusyChannel) with a context of their own, made from
context.Background(), which ends when the channel clears and never with
the dial's (waitIfBusy in wl2k-go's ardop and in Pat-Vara). An abort
(/api/disconnect, the mailbox's Abort) while that wait's prompt was
open was logged ("Got abort signal while dialing varahf,
cancelling..."), and the wait went on until the prompt's 5 minutes were
up: VARA HF's Connect returned only then ("aborted while waiting for
clear channel"), and the next connection could not go before. ARDOP's
Connect returns at once, but left its dial waiting in the background,
the prompt open (which holds back the next prompt, the password's), and
called the gateway when the channel cleared.

Connect now keeps its dial's context for the busy function
(busy_abort.go), and onBusyChannel ends with it too: an abort ends the
wait and its prompt (the mailbox and APP > Mail are told it is gone)
and the dial, as the prompt's own Abort does, and a wait that only
begins after its Connect returned (ARDOP's background dial) ends at
once. Connect logs "Connect cancelled" for it, as for an abort at any
other point of the dial, where VARA HF's dialer gave its own error. The
prompt's Abort and Continue answers, the channel clearing and the 5
minute timeout do as before.

The fix belongs in the two dialers (the dial's context given to the
busy function); this is Pat's side of it, without changing them.

With tests (app/busy_abort_test.go): the wait and its prompt, and
Connect through a stand-in VARA HF modem and a stand-in ARDOP TNC on
loopback, the channel busy: the abort ends Connect at once, and the
next connection prompts and calls, once.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
